            "description": "Watch Exeter City vs Bradford City highlights and goals from League One on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on May 2, 2026. Late Drama Defines League One Clash In a highly anticipated League One fixture held on May 2, 2026, Exeter City and Bradford City faced off in a match defined by tactical grit and late-game desperation. The encounter proved to be a challenging test for both sides, with the momentum shifting significantly during the final exchanges. Controlling the Tempo The match began with high physical intensity, as players fought hard for every ball, resulting in a series of disciplinary actions early on. Bradford City drew first blood in the 27th minute when Kayden Jackson clinically finished a setup from George Lapslie . Throughout the remainder of the first half and into the second, the visitors managed to stifle the home side's offensive efforts while looking for chances to double their lead. The Final Surge As the game entered its closing phase, Antoni Sarcevic struck in the 79th minute to put Bradford City in a commanding position. The home crowd roared when Josh Magennis scored in the 90+3rd minute, courtesy of a Ryan Rydel assist, but it was too little, too late. Despite the frantic energy in stoppage time, the visitors managed to hold on to their lead and walk away with the victory."
